    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-11640",
      "knowledge_point_id": "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix",
      "problem": "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $BC=CB={I}_{2}$\n- $BD=DB={I}_{2}$\n- $D={B}^{-1}$",
      "worked_solution": "- First, we check whether $BC=CB={I}_{2}.$ Computing $BC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 4 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false.\n\n- Now, we check whether $BD=DB={I}_{2}.$ Computing $BD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BD & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DB & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true. As a result, $D={B}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
